{
  "title": "Phase 3: serverless Ghost (compact, per function group)",
  "description": "Serverless Ghost on AWS. CloudFront serves the site from a content bucket and sends dynamic paths to an HTTP API that fronts the Lambda functions. Functions read and write a SQLite database kept in an S3 bucket. Posts are rendered to static pages by a queue-driven generator (failed messages go to a dead-letter queue); EventBridge Scheduler runs the recurring and one-shot background jobs. Newsletters are sent through Mailgun, staff sign-in mail through an SMTP provider, and credentials are read from Parameter Store. CloudWatch alarms notify an email topic. A deploy bucket holds the code the functions are updated from.",
